    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sublustris</span></b> , e, adj.
		sub-lux, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>giving some light</i>, <i>having a
				faint light</i>, <i>glimmering</i> (not
			ante-Aug., and very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 27, 31</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 5, 47</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">umbra (noctis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 373</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 3, 141</span></i>.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eloquentiae Latinae lumina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 13, 24, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
